## Known issues intentionally left open

- The actual Windows RC2 acceptance report showed the reported screenshot's damage ambiguity (`873131` versus `87373`). The existing candidate-selection logic remains fail-closed. The new helper code has unit coverage, but its effect on real OCR has **not** been evaluated on the current source because the OCR dependencies are unavailable here.
- Hoffmann, Libertad, and Schlieffen's XP/Free XP issues are addressed by a geometry-based repair attempt, but this is not yet validated against those real screenshots. Credits can also trigger geometry rereads when the current value has an extra suffix digit.
- Map prefix cleanup now has regression tests, but the whole screenshot suite still needs to prove exact map extraction on Windows.
- Libertad's `O`/`0` player-name confusion remains unresolved. Do not force a canonical spelling from cross-screenshot ground truth; inspect high-confidence identity candidates before changing consensus.
- Reported-screenshot PSM 11 damage candidate formation still needs inspection in a live current-source JSON report. Existing consensus behavior is covered by unit tests, but that Windows-specific reading has not been reproduced here.
- First/middle/final recognition-pass stall injection has not been added yet. Keep it gated until the new source passes the isolated lifecycle check and the current-source OCR accuracy fixtures. The historical pass-16 root cause remains unknown.
- Windows native Tesseract (`tesseract.exe`) comparison and authorized live Discord smoke testing remain independent release gates.

